// cross_mod_array_widen_arg — pins the imported exact-match semantics
// (.nmod v1.12 type descriptors). The consumer-side stub rebuilds BOTH
// formals of `int sum2(int[] a, float b)` from the serialized recursive
// type descriptors, so both bindings are exact: no per-binding fixup
// runs, `b` keeps 2.5 across the call, and the exit code is 3.
// (Pre-v1.12 the stub degraded both formals to int placeholders and the
// fixup re-read the float slot as int bits — a denormal — exit code 1.)
int sum2(int[] a, float b) {
    if (a != null && b > 2) return 3;
    return 1;
}
